course: dictionary
lesson: 11937
title: Candlelight
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Candlelight is a compound word, made of two smaller words you already know: candle and light. Break it apart and the meaning often appears. A candle gives light, so candlelight is the light that comes from a candle or candles.
explain: «The old farmhouse had no electricity, so the family ate their supper by candlelight.» The clue is no electricity. Candlelight is the light people used instead, and it is soft and warm, not bright like a lamp.
explain: Candlelight is also linked to special, quiet moments. «The church held a carol service by candlelight at Christmas.» «The town held a candlelight vigil to remember the people who had died.» In these sentences, candlelight helps make the mood calm and thoughtful.
explain: Candlelight is uncountable, so you say «some candlelight», not «two candlelights». To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: «by the soft light from a candle» still makes sense.
fact: Candlelight means the soft light from a candle or candles.
fact: «Candlelight» is a compound word: «candle» + «light».
fact: Before electricity, people read, worked and cooked by candlelight.
fact: A candlelight vigil is a gathering where people hold candles to remember someone.
fact: Candlelight is uncountable: you say «some candlelight», not «two candlelights».
exercise: «The room was lit only by candlelight.» What does candlelight mean? | A loud noise made by a candle | A bright light from a torch | *The soft light from a candle | A cold wind through an open window
exercise: «The villagers held a candlelight vigil for the lost fishermen.» What was the vigil for? | To start a race | *To remember people who had died | To celebrate a birthday with a big party | To sell candles at the market
exercise: Which two smaller words make up candlelight? | can and dlight | candle and night | candy and lite | *candle and light
test: «They read their books by candlelight until the candle burned low.» Where does the candlelight come from? | *A candle | The moon | The sun | An electric lamp
test: Which is true about candlelight? | It is always made by electricity | *It is soft light from a candle or candles | It is a kind of tall tree | It is a loud, bright noise
exam: «The carol service was held by candlelight, and everyone sang softly.» What does «by candlelight» tell us about the service? | It was lit by the glow of a bright lamp | It was held outside in the sunshine | It was held in total darkness with no light at all | *It was lit by the soft light of candles
